Welcome to the Ohio Bees Github folder!

This is a file created by Caralee Shepard on 1/3/2025 to explain the contents of this github folder. 

This paper was the result of compiling data from three papers, and several years of data analysis as we reinterpreted the data in a new way. The project design changed over time, and the various folders left behind leave homage to the various iterations of the project. We are not removing the ones we did not use, in hopes that they may be useful to later researchers.

I am going in alphabetical order of explaining the files here, rather than date of most recent modification. (This should technically be the first file you see, but 1 starts directly under it)

1) Analysiswithoutseasonalbeestest - a folder created to run the final regional to urban species pool analysis, with 12 species removed that may not have been possible to collect based on historical seasonality and sampling timeframes for the three projects. This folder is used for the creation of supplemental materials, and the full versions of all local analyses are in file #22.

2) bcomm_23.localanalysis.csv (and xlsx) - the files that contain the presence absence data for each species in the regional species pool at each sites sampled during the 3 studies used to create the urban species pool

3) Bees.of.Cleveland- the functional traits associated with the species found by our studies in Cleveland. Was not used as part of analysis, but is essentially file #4 with the extra bees removed- however it did not save with the species names.

4) btraits_23.csv and (and xlsx) - these files are the functional traits associated with every bee species in the regional species pool. The functional traits are represented numerically so they can be used for statistical analysis. For the key to which numbers correspond to which traits see file #5.

5) Categorical Trait key for analysis v3.csv - the functional trait categories and the associated numbers used to represent them in our functional analysis. best read if opened as an excel file. 

6) Figures - This folder contains a folder with figures used for the manuscript (as well as the adobe indesign projects used to make labels and add significance indicators to each figure, etc), a folder with all the various unused figures from this project, the workspace used to create the figures and code for creating some of the local panel figures. 

7) Final Local analysis - this code is the beginning code for performing local analyses of comparing the urban species pool across the different urban habitat types. use it until around line 85 which has the warning that you should then go to each project's code file (see files #8, #9, and #10)

8) Final_Local_FS.R - R code used to do the urban species pool to local habitat analysis of the species found in Sivakoff et al 2018 habitats. 

9) Final_Local_KT.R - R code used to do the urban species pool to local habitat analysis of the species found in Turo et al 2021 habitats. 

10) Final_Local_MP.R - R code used to do the urban species pool to local habitat analysis of the species found in Pham et al in review habitats. 

11)FinalRegional_workspace.RData- The R workspace used to save previous analyses during regional analysis so each line of code did not have to be run each time.

12) landscape.localanalysis.csv - a file containing habitat treatment and landscape data for each site sampled as part of the three projects. Mostly anecdotal data as landscape data was dropped as part of the analysis, and the file still contains data for C8 which was dropped from analysis (see file #21)

13) LocalFS.workspace.RData - The R workspace used to save previous analyses during the local analysis of Sivakoff et al 2018 so each line of code did not have to be run each time.

14) LocalFS.workspace.RData - The R workspace used to save previous analyses during the local analysis of Turo et al 2021 so each line of code did not have to be run each time.

15) LocalFS.workspace.RData - The R workspace used to save previous analyses during the local analysis of Pham et al in review so each line of code did not have to be run each time.

16) Ohio_Bee_Project.Rproj - the r project connected to the git folder.

17) Pre.2.23_reruns - In February 2023 a mistake was discovered in one of the data sets (ie one species was marked as absent when it was captured as part of one of the studies or vice versa) and so I put all the previous data runs into this folder and then went through every matrix to check for any other mistakes before rerunning analyses.

18) Rao.function.R - The R code for the Rao function, run before doing any null model analyses.

19) README.md - a file created when the Git folder was created.

20) Regional to Urban_Null models_Hillsmith_3 Axes- an earlier version of the regional analysis null from file #22 that were run when only two papers (Sivakoff et al 2018 and Turo et al 2021) were being included in the urban species pool. 

21) Regional to Urban_Null models_Hillsmith_3 AxeswC8 - an earlier version of the regional analysis nulls that were run in file #20 when the site C8 was included in the analysis. C8 was removed because it was not vacuumed.

22) Regional to Urbban_Nulls_FINAL - the null models created by the regional species pool anlaysis with all three paper data sets included. 

23) Regional to Urban.R - The code used to run the analyses creating null models of the regional species pool to compare to the urban species pool created from the three paper's data.

24)SES.csv - a file created of all SES values created as part of the regional to urban null model analyses (in file #23).

25) traits_urbanpool.csv - the file of the functional traits for species found in Clevleand, used as part of the local analysis (in file #7).

26) Undifferentiated_local_analyses - a file of code used in earlier data analyses for the urban to local analysis stage, when local analyses were not divided by paper. It was determined that all habitats could not be compared against eachother due to different sampling methods, so these codes were modified in their newer forms (Files #7-10). Also contains folders with the resulting null models from the varius earlier stages of analysis. 

27) Urban to Local_Nulls_FS - Null model analyses created based on the urban species pool compared to the bees collected in each site that was part of Sivakoff et al 2018. 

28) Urban to Local_Nulls_KT - Null model analyses created based on the urban species pool compared to the bees collected in each site that was part of Turo et al 2021.

29) Urban to Local_Nulls_MP - Null model analyses created based on the urban species pool compared to the bees collected in each site that was part of Pham et al in review.

30) urbanpool.FS.csv - The sites from Sivakoff et al 2018 and the members of the urban species pool that were present and absent at each. 

31) urbanpool.KT.csv - The sites from Turo et al 2021 and the members of the urban species pool that were present and absent at each. 

32) urbanpool.MP.csv - The sites from Pham et al in review and the members of the urban species pool that were present and absent at each. 